Release 1.1.5 Windows executable icon cache correction.

Observed failure:
- Release workflow 32709673765 built macOS and Linux successfully, but Windows failed its installed-state inspection with the bounded category installed-brand.
- The previous hardcoded validator hash exactly matched frame 0 of the old 32x32 ICO, while the current source ICO has a different frame hash.

Root cause:
- Pinned tauri-build 2.6.3 reads icons/icon.ico and embeds it with tauri-winres, but only emits Cargo rerun directives for configuration files and resources, not for the chosen ICO.
- A restored Cargo target can therefore link the previous Windows resource after an icon-only branding change.

Correction:
- src-tauri/build.rs now explicitly emits cargo:rerun-if-changed=icons/icon.ico before tauri_build::build().
- The reason is documented at the decision site.
- The package migration contract requires the exact invalidation directive before the Tauri build call; removing it makes the test fail.

Verification:
- npm run test:package-migration: red before correction, then 6/6 passed.
- npm run test:release-workflow: 39/39 passed.
- cargo fmt --all --check: passed.
- cargo check: passed.
- cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings: passed.
- git diff --check: passed.
